    Cover the header's bottom margin while it grows back near the top
    
    The compact header keeps the page in place with a bottom margin the size
    of the height it lost. When the header grows back while the page is
    scrolled less than that margin (scrolling or jumping up to the top), the
    bar is still shorter than the space it holds open, and that strip showed
    straight through to the section background, opening a gap between the
    header and the TOC sidebar.
    
    .pf-page::before fills the strip with the header's glass. It sits in the
    page at the margin's position and size, so it is 0px tall when the
    header is expanded and scrolls away under the stuck header otherwise.

