Author: Kyle Tanglao <ktanglao@lsu.edu>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 02:34:19 2026 +0000

    Hold the compact header until the TOC sidebar can follow it
    
    A sticky element never moves above its place in the page. The TOC
    sidebar's place is below the expanded header and the breadcrumb, so when
    the header shrank after the fixed 4rem of scroll, the sidebar could not
    yet rise to the compact bar and a gap opened under the header until the
    page scrolled further.
    
    palefireCompactAfter measures the sidebar's place and the compact bar
    height (on a hidden copy of the header) and lengthens the scroll
    sentinel to the distance the sidebar needs. $pf-header-compact-after is
    now the minimum.

