Author: Kyle Tanglao <ktanglao@lsu.edu>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 02:21:24 2026 +0000

    Keep TOC sidebar in sync with the shrinking sticky header
    
    The sidebar's sticky top comes from --pf-header-h, which a ResizeObserver
    updated from the bar's content box. The compact transition animates the
    bar's padding, which content-box observation does not report, so the
    sidebar lagged by that padding and only caught up at the 400ms re-measure.
    
    Observe the border box, measure unrounded heights, and re-measure on every
    animation frame while the header shrinks or grows.

